From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wlan: gen4m: mt6789: no EMI MPU change around firmware load

The MT6789 platform code implements kalSetEmiMpuProtection() as an
empty function, but only under CONFIG_MTK_EMI. Without MediaTek's EMI
driver the weak default in gl_kal.c ran instead and logged "EMI MPU
function is not defined" with a WARN class on every firmware download
and power-up.

MediaTek's MT6789 implementation does nothing even when its EMI driver
is present, so there is nothing missing to warn about. Build it
unconditionally.
---
--- a/wlan_drv_gen4m_6789/os/linux/plat/mt6789/plat_priv.c
+++ b/wlan_drv_gen4m_6789/os/linux/plat/mt6789/plat_priv.c
@@ -201,11 +201,11 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
-#ifdef CONFIG_MTK_EMI
 void kalSetEmiMpuProtection(phys_addr_t emiPhyBase, bool enable)
 {
 }
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_MTK_EMI
 void kalSetDrvEmiMpuProtection(phys_addr_t emiPhyBase, uint32_t offset,
 			       uint32_t size)
 {
